{"study_accession":"PRJNA312538","secondary_study_accession":"SRP070532","title":"miR-126 Orchestrates an Oncogenic Program in B-Cell Precursor Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia","description":"MicroRNA (miRNA)-126 is a known regulator of hematopoietic stem cell quiescence. We engineered murine hematopoiesis to express miRNA-126 across all differentiation stages. Thirty percent of mice developed monoclonal B cell leukemia, which was prevented or regressed when a tetracycline-repressible miRNA-126 cassette was switched off. Regression was accompanied by upregulation of cell-cycle regulators and B cell differentiation genes, and downregulation of oncogenic signaling pathways. Expression of dominant-negative p53 delayed blast clearance upon miRNA-126 switch-off, highlighting the relevance of p53 inhibition in miRNA-126 addiction. Forced miRNA-126 expression in mouse and human progenitors reduced p53 transcriptional activity through regulation of multiple p53-related targets. miRNA-126 is highly expressed in a subset of human B-ALL, and antagonizing miRNA-126 in ALL xenograft models triggered apoptosis and reduced disease burden. Overall design: Study 1: Turning off miR-126 expression from an experimental murine B-ALL in vivo; Study 2: Modulation of miR-126 expression in human cord blood stem and progenitor cell populations in vitro.","pubmed":"27300437","geo_series":"","n_samples":18,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN04503124","study_accession":"PRJNA312538","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"huCB stem ctrl_rep1","description":"huCB stem ctrl_rep1","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM2066393","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2016-06-15","attributes":[["source_name","huCB stem ctrl"],["cell_type","human cord blood HSPC (CD34+CD133+CD38-)"],["genotype","control vector"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR3178284","experiment_accession":"SRX1592574","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina HiSeq 2500","rea